          "message": {
            "text": "Organization-only RLS permits inconsistent cross-tenant relationship tuples\n\nChild tables authorize only organization_id while accepting independent related-object IDs, permitting mixed-tenant tuples.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Authorization bypass tenant integrity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-639\n\nRemediation:\nAdd composite tenant foreign keys and RLS checks for every related object.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject the negative path for composite-tenant-binding.\n- Preserve the intended bounded path.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant in a shared database or admission control.\n- Add a negative regression test for the direct path."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:8e294d4fffffc22acf684619caf1f6fa037f88f95e46c28b69a6030a765f4f51"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Authorization bypass / tenant integrity",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_44d1529d7c4559355db37fe1",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_0a238d2d74e8ffd0548f9be5",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "tenant-integrity.related-object-binding",
          "ruleIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
