          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Workspace provisioning can create duplicate organizations and sites\n\nConcurrent first-use calls can duplicate organizations and same-name sites through select-then-insert.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Race condition tenant provisioning\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-362\n\nRemediation:\nAdd idempotency keys, uniqueness, and transactional provisioning.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject the negative path for workspace-provisioning-race.\n- Preserve the intended bounded path.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant in a shared database or admission control.\n- Add a negative regression test for the direct path."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:644d0bbee0a8366456cc7b5e86eeaebb3d3011350539a82de81d0090c2ae4e2b"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "Race condition / tenant provisioning",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_f75d6f1cd78d8c433440f49c",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_a5ee75b432e9149097c869f7",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "race-condition.workspace-provisioning",
          "ruleIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "source"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/api/share-sessions/%5BsessionId%5D/route.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 130,
                  "startLine": 79
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "sink"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/workpack-commercial-store.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 449,
                  "startLine": 320
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Public Share documents treat tenant object identifiers as recipient credentials\n\nUnauthenticated GET uses sessionId plus workerId membership as sufficient authority to return workpack documents.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Authorization bypass public Share\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-639\n\nRemediation:\nRequire recipient-specific random or signed short-lived invitation proof.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject the negative path for share-id-credential.\n- Preserve the intended bounded path.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant in a shared database or admission control.\n- Add a negative regression test for the direct path."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:aa430029cb82f2dd75f1a3907ab5efa26773e6409fecdca80bf8b0df93643c03"
