                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Weather fallback responses still expose raw upstream error text\n\nProvider errors become successful fallback signal details despite route-level catch redaction.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Information exposure error handling\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-209\n\nRemediation:\nLog raw provider failures server-side and return fixed fallback messages or enumerated public codes.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Inject raw provider error and assert response omits it.\n- Cover every provider branch.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Separate internal diagnostics from DTOs.\n- Use a shared public projection."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:94a1d90014911b0de78b0cb9acfe2e4bec01cbd03ce8f92ecc2a1f18ba3d6712"
